---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { vonar } from '../../data/vonar';

// Answers follow the Vonar README, CONTRIBUTING.md and release notes.
const { installer } = vonar;
const issuesUrl = `${vonar.repoUrl}/issues`;
---

<Page
  title="Vonar FAQ – SmartScreen, macOS, presets and more · Xami"
  description="Answers about the free Vonar synth: why Windows SmartScreen warns you, checking the download, macOS support, other DAWs, where your presets are saved."
  eyebrow="FAQ"
  heading="Questions."
  headingMuted="Short answers."
>
  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="free">Is Vonar really free?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. No account, no licence key, nothing to unlock. You can use it in your music, also commercially. The music
      and sounds you make with Vonar are yours. The plugin itself is free software under the{' '}
      <a href={vonar.licenseUrl}>AGPLv3</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="smartscreen">Why does Windows SmartScreen warn me?</h2>
    <p>
      The installer is not signed with a paid code-signing certificate, so Windows does not recognise the publisher
      yet. Click <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. The
      <a href={`${vonar.guidePath}#smartscreen`}>installation guide</a> shows each step.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="sha256">How do I check that my download is genuine?</h2>
    <p>Open PowerShell in your Downloads folder and run:</p>
    <pre><code>Get-FileHash .\{installer.fileName} -Algorithm SHA256</code></pre>
    <p>The result must be:</p>
    <pre><code>{installer.sha256}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Official downloads are only available from this site and the GitHub repository. Any other site is
      unofficial.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="macos">Does Vonar work on macOS?</h2>
    <p>
      No. Vonar is a 64-bit (x64) VST3 plugin for {vonar.platform}. There is no macOS build and no ARM64 build.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="daws">Does it work in DAWs other than FL Studio?</h2>
    <p>
      Vonar is a standard VST3 plugin and installs into <code>C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3</code>, where
      every DAW looks for plugins. FL Studio is the main target and the host it is tested in by hand.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="fl-presets">Why are the presets not in FL Studio's preset menu?</h2>
    <p>
      Vonar has its own preset bar at the top of its window: click the preset name to open the menu grouped by
      category. The plugin gives FL Studio a single “program”, so FL Studio's own preset list stays empty. Your
      sound, preset name and macro labels are still saved in the project.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="user-presets">Where are my own presets saved?</h2>
    <p>
      Presets you save with <strong>SAVE</strong> are JSON files in <code>%APPDATA%\Vonar\Presets</code>. You can
      copy them to another computer; afterwards choose <em>Rescan user presets</em> in the preset menu.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="volt">I used VOLT before. What changed?</h2>
    <p>
      Vonar was called VOLT during development. The installer removes the old <code>VOLT.vst3</code> so FL Studio
      does not list the plugin twice. Projects made with VOLT open in Vonar with their sounds, and your presets are
      copied over automatically.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="uninstall">How do I uninstall it?</h2>
    <p>Open <strong>Settings → Apps</strong> in Windows and uninstall Vonar.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="share">Can I share my presets?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. Presets are the only contributions accepted for now. See <a href={vonar.contributingUrl}>how to submit a
      preset</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2 id="bug">I found a bug. Where do I report it?</h2>
    <p>Open an <a href={issuesUrl}>issue on GitHub</a>. Ideas are welcome there too.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
